  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MELCA  2013-15 (17-18):Gambella Biosphere Reserve - M &amp; E Support to MELCA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">MELCA  2013-15 (17-18):Gambella Biosphere Reserve</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Manjang Biosphere reserve&#xa0;project strategized to adopt the internationally recognized Man and the Biosphere program approach where the MFBR nominated, registered and managed by collaborative effort of the government and community in the area.
These reserves promote conservation solutions and work to preserve biodiversity through a focus on sustainability. Biospheres aim to reconcile environmental conservation with economic development through scientific research and community education.
Biospheres lead to harmonic co-existence of local communities with culture and local surrounding and provide opportunities for conserving nature through the sustainable use of natural resources.
Biospheres are created with the goal of accomplishing three basic functions:
Conservation function 
Biosphere reserves aim to contribute to the preservation of landscapes, ecosystems, species and genetic variation
Development function 
Biosphere reserves aim to foster economic development which is socio-culturally and ecologically sustainable
Logistic function 
Provide support for research, monitoring, education and information exchange related to local, national and global issues of conservation and development</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let med projektet &#xe4;r lokalsamh&#xe4;llets h&#xe5;llbara utveckling och fr&#xe4;mjandet av den lokala biologiska och kulturella m&#xe5;ngfalden i Majang zonen i Gambella regionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is improved sustainable community development and local bio-cultural diversity in Majang zone in Gambella region.</narrative>
  </description>
